# This is an example configuration file for Claude Code.
#
# --- ⚠️ SECURITY WARNING ---
# Storing your password in a plaintext file is a major security risk.
# Anyone who gains access to this file will have your password.
#
# A safer alternative is to configure the `/etc/sudoers` file to allow
# specific commands to be run without a password.
#
# This file is provided for demonstration purposes only.
# USE AT YOUR OWN RISK.
#
# --- Instructions ---
# 1. Copy this file to your home directory:
#    cp .claude_code_config.example ~/.claude_code_config
#
# 2. Secure the file by making it readable only by you:
#    chmod 600 ~/.claude_code_config
#
# 3. Edit the new file (~/.claude_code_config) and enter your password.

# --- Sudo Password ---
SUDO_PASSWORD="your_password_here"
